  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia: Somalia Justice Support Programme (SOMJUST)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) The Judicial Training Institute (JTI) offers continuous legal educational opportunities to judicial personnel at federal and Federal Member State (FMS) levels. 2) Federal and FMS prosecutors adopt an operational framework for the coordinated investigation and prosecution of complex crimes. 3) Federal and FMS prosecutors know how to carry out their functions in a coordinated way and in line with national and international standards. 4) Organizational and management capacities of MCP strengthened. 5) MCP staff maintain up-to-date records and share timely information with the relevant criminal justice chain actors including police, prosecutors, and courts. 6) The Somalia Bar Association (SBA) effectively exercises its oversight function in legal education. 7) SBA practicing lawyers know how to represent criminal cases in court. 8) Somali criminal justice actors know how to professionally conduct forensic investigations. 9) Key policymakers at federal and FMS levels agree on a joint vision for the revised Criminal Procedure Code.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: JTI, federal and FMS Attorney General&#x2019;s Offices and Chief Justice Offices, the Ministry of Justice (MOJ) of the Federal Government of Somalia (particularly the Policy and Legislative Drafting Unit (PLDU), federal and FMS judges, prosecutors, and court clerks; selected investigators; the Custodial Corps (especially the MCP), the SBA, prospective and practitioners; the Bureau of Forensic Science. Indirect beneficiaries: Entire criminal justice chain in Somalia, including justice seekers.Indirect beneficiaries: Entire criminal justice chain in Somalia, including justice seekers.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enable Somalia criminal justice institutions to deliver effective, efficient, accessible, and accountable justice services to Somali citizens.</narrative>
  </description>
